<title>HONG KONG: Credit Lyonnais to withdraw CEPA warrants.</title>
<headline>Credit Lyonnais to withdraw CEPA warrants.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Lyonnais Financial Products (Guernsey) Ltd said on Monday it would apply to suspend trading in its 380 million call warrants on Consolidated Electric Power Asia Ltd (CEPA) on December 11 and plans to withdraw the warrant on December 30.</p>
<p>Holders exercising their warrants before November 29, will be entitled to receive CEPA shares, while holders exercising warrants between November 29 to December 11 will receive cash in lieu of shares, CL said.</p>
<p>In October, CEPA parent Hopewell Holdings Ltd announced that it was selling a controlling stake in CEPA to Southern Co of the U.S. in a move which could lead to the privatisation and delisting of CEPA.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
